t['criteria'] = 'Two things. (1) On that walk, did any tree fail to update, flicker, pop, or light wrongly while you walked and turned? Say yes or no, and what if yes. (2) If no: say whether to make it the default (it is still off unless the URL flag is on). The forest’s shadow pass is not covered by it yet, which is a separate, smaller item.'
t['outcome'] = (t.get('outcome', '') + ' 23:43 and 23:44: two flag-on walks, and this time it skipped: no refusals, main scene 114 of 214 and 114 of 220 refreshed (100 to 106 forest meshes skipped per render). Measured, same capture kind as the controls: the bindings stage p50 2.3 to 2.5 ms against 4.1 to 4.3 with it off, the node-update stage 2.1 to 2.3 against 4.6 to 5.1, the main scene’s last-frame encode 6 to 7 ms against 14 to 19. Cross-run, loosely: frame p50 19 to 20 ms against 28 to 31, fps 49 to 52 against 34 to 36; you moved a larger share of those captures (97 per cent of frames against 87 to 94), so the frame figure is if anything conservative. The sun’s shadow pass still refreshed all 32 of its objects: Three renders it with its own override depth material, which the policy does not reach.').strip()
d['updatedAt'] = '2026-09-10T23:55:00.000Z'
